From ebcacff3575e76260d03f8818ec723b24875b874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:57:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: the build tree's <name>.log, so roottest's sibling log
 checks run

RootTestDriver.cmake writes every ROOT_ADD_TEST test's output to
$CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR/<testname>.log (its OUTPUT), and roottest's
schemaEvolution checks sed a sibling's schemaRun1.log out of that same
directory. The harness kept the output in OUT/logs only, so the reference
test died on 'sed: schemaRun1.log: No such file or directory' and its four
checks were blocked behind it.

A Test now records the log the driver writes (outlog, from ROOTTEST_ADD_TEST's
name in its directory) and the runner writes it into the working copy before
judging, with the output already through OUTCNVCMD/OUTCNV as the driver
converts before writing. An OUTREF spelled <build>/... is a file a test of the
same run wrote in the build tree, so it is read from the working copy rather
than searched for below ROOT's sources.

roottest/root/treeformula/schemaEvolution/{schemaRun2,2a,4,4a}check: FAIL ->
PASS, and reference with them.
---
